"settings.thresholdCaption" = "In one-direction mode, utterances whose mean recognition confidence is below this value are not translated and appear as \"translation skipped\" (this filters out mis-recognitions of other languages, e.g. side chatter in the room). In the bidirectional and bilingual modes it is the adoption floor of the language judgment: a finalized result below it is treated as the wrong-language recognizer's misreading and discarded entirely — neither shown nor saved. Takes effect immediately. Confidence is also recorded in the saved JSONL, so you can tune it with real data.";
